{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfun22PvrsuC7PPrctX6m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not really. When a new version is deployed, Cloudflare restarts running Durable Object instances so they pick up the new code. In-flight requests get a short grace period to finish, but you can't configure an object to keep running the old version for an extended time.\n\nThe closest option is **gradual deployments** (`wrangler versions upload` followed by `wrangler versions deploy` with percentage splits). Durable Objects support these. Each object ID is deterministically pinned to one version, so you can keep most objects on the old code and move them over in stages. Any object whose assigned version changes is still restarted at that point.\n\nDesign your objects to tolerate restarts: persist state to storage, and make alarms and WebSocket handling resumable (for example, with the Hibernation API)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2258,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2258},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00ef7dff-d01b-4e23-b504-7d48c8e172af","uuid":"83709171-f8c8-4796-9808-12172e9efab8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:56:46.492Z","request_id":"req_011Cfun22CXdzwnu6mFcfXYo"}
